What: capture_rt_priority=0 (default off) or 1..20 requests Linux FIFO for
only the asynchronous capture thread, with SCHED_RESET_ON_FORK. Parse strict
integers, disable on invalid input, and log/continue on EPERM or other errors.
Operational policy and first-frame monotonic markers once per capture thread;
no per-frame timing probes or observer files.
No service-wide RT policy, affinity change, wrapper TID guessing or SYS_NICE.
Status: experimental opt-in scheduling policy, potentially upstreamable.
Evidence: /tmp/h700-sun/convert.md scheduling section (2026-10-22): capture
FIFO 15 delivered 600 new acquisitions in every one of 27 strict 10 s windows.
CPU3 isolation was rejected. Lower-priority work can still be delayed.
Removal: equivalent upstream capture policy, lost need, or responsiveness /
starvation evidence. Native LimitRTPRIO is a separate explicit host approval.

